ck to  his old life and she's basically asking  him whether he misses it or not we cut  away from this being in the office  before we get to find out if Christa  knows about his alternate personality  there we see Elliot returning home and  he addresses the audience for the first  time he says he knows we want to know  what he told Christa but he doesn't  trust us enough at this point he says  that we've kept information from him and  then when he goes inside we see mr.  robot for the first time in his room we  get a closer look at what he is  journaling and learned that he is  documenting everything that is happening  mr. robot is telling that telling him  that they still have work to do and that  a revolution needs a leader Elliot asked  mr. robot to tell more Tyrell is and mr.  robot says he can't do that  Elliot then tells him to go [ __ ] himself  and mr. robot uses the gun from the  popcorn machine to shoot him in the head  he falls back but he gets right back up  so you can tell that it's just some sort  of internal conflict we learned from the  journal that this is a recurring  recurring part of the loop like he's  shot in before but it isn't clear if it  happens every day or if mr. robot always  says the same things from there we get a  short scene with a character who looks  like Darlene wearing an F Society mask  she's on a mission to cut the balls off  the bull statue on Wall Street then we  cut to a new character and hearing her  up  go home then having problems with her  security alarm from there we see that  her smart home system is acting like it  has a mind of its own everything she  tries to do basically it just switches  back or you know she's trying to take a  shower and the water goes the water  temperature goes up really hot  she turns off the stereo the stereo  comes back on things like that she  realized that it's glitching out and  after calling the company she decides to  leave and stay at another house that she  hasn't Greenwich  as soon a